• **The blind-round ledger, by hand.** This changed a routing decision: round 66 is 3/3 and round 58 is 4/4 → close their receipts, but round 57 is 1 of 3 graded. The gate is green on it (partial = warning) and the round is still owed two grades — so #796 stays open. Closing it on a green suite would be the "could not check → checked; clean" reading I refuse everywhere else.

